      "verdict_rationale": "Issue: the runner verifies the Clifford and C_3 algebra and exhaustively classifies selectors already satisfying swap invariance, but it does not derive the implication from \u201corientation-free derivability\u201d to f\u2218tau=f. Why this blocks: the two-model witness establishes an orientation ambiguity in the underlying real presentation, not a formal naturality theorem governing every admissible selector. Repair target: specify the selector language and prove its constructions commute with the conjugation automorphism. Claim boundary until fixed: conditional on f\u2218tau=f, doublet constancy and the two-block finest fixed-label fiber partition are exact; N1/N7 leave the naturality route unresolved, N2 finds that single obstruction, N3 finds no additional hidden premise, N4 has no prior-witness residual, N5 finds no stronger resolution-complete no-go, N6 supplies no registered closure, and N8 supplies no applicable retirement echo."
